# Login Page Redesign — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- High-level goal: Redesign the IQArchive login page to match the user-provided reference mockup, featuring a high-impact split-screen layout with the Bicol University monument on the left and a clean DaisyUI card on the right.
- Scope: 
  - Left hero panel: Bicol University entrance monument with deep navy gradient overlay, orange workspace badge line, crisp white typography with highlighted orange "Quality Assurance" span, and descriptive mission text.
  - Right auth panel: Clean white background with centered elevated DaisyUI card, Bicol University seal, IQArchive title, Google Workspace SSO button, support link, and padlock security footer.
  - Preserved security logic: Google OAuth redirect (`/auth/google/redirect`), `@bicol-u.edu.ph` error feedback alerts, and desktop viewport guard (`<MobileUnsupported />`).
  - Standalone preview: Production HTML/CSS preview in `docs/designs/login/index.html`.
- Key decisions:
  - Use DaisyUI card, alert, and button classes adhering strictly to `daisyui.md` and `DESIGN.md`.
  - Use official Bicol University Orange `#F26522` and Navy `#0B1B3D` tokens.
  - Modular, concise code keeping `Login.vue` under 160 lines per general rules.
- Edge cases to handle:
  - Error/Info/Success alert banners from OAuth callback.
  - Responsive collapse for viewports below 1024px via `MobileUnsupported.vue`.
  - Image scaling on varied desktop aspect ratios (`object-cover`, `bg-cover`, `bg-center`).
- Testing strategy:
  - Standalone HTML rendering check.
  - Vue build validation via `npm run build`.
  - PHPUnit test suite: `php artisan test --filter=GoogleAuthTest`.
  - Browser subagent visual inspection of `http://127.0.0.1:8000/login`.

